When it becomes too difficult to move the shrubs apart with your hands, you take a long hand-made machete, reminiscent of the kind comic book heroes wield, out of your backpack. You made the machete with your dad, just for fun. Your father grumbled all the time that such a knife is not a toy for kids. Probably, now he would be glad for you. You fancy yourself as an adventurer, who ventures through the jungle in search of treasure. You make good progress, and soon you catch glimpses of the lake through gaps between the bushes, the lake that you are heading for.
Finally, the last bushes give way under your pressure, and with a sense of relief, you step onto the oozy shore of the lake, leaving the thick shrubbery behind.